div0.entryFree:
λάγν-ευμα,ατος,τό,
coition, Hp. Nat.Puer. 31 ;
semen, Id. Int. 47 .

λαίβα: ἀσπίς, τρίβων, πέλτη, Hsch.
λαίγματα: πέμματα, οἱ δὲ σπέρματα, ἱερὰ ἀπάργματα, Id., cf. Cyr. , Phot. (λάγμ-);
v. λαῖμα .

λᾰμῠρ-ία,ἡ, (
λαμυρός
111
)
wantonness, of women, Plu. Sull. 35 , Luc. 6 ; of a man, Id. Ant. 24 ;
pertness, Id. 2.66c , 1124b .

λᾰπ-ίζω,
= συρίζω , S. Fr. 1062 ;
swagger, rodomontade, Cic. Att. 9.13.4 , AB 277 , Phot. ; cf.λαοπίζειν.

λεληθότως,Adv. pf. part.ofλανθάνω,
imperceptibly, Pl. Ax. 365c , Cic. Att. 6.5.3 , Fam. 9.2.3 , D.H. Comp. 22 , Anacreont. 15.16 , Luc. Am. 13 ;
secretly, LXX 2 Ma. 6.11 , 8.1 .

λεοντ-ιάω,
suffer from ἐλεφαντίασις, Id.l.c.;
to be like a lion, Tz. H. 4.937 .

λεπῡ́ρ-ιον,τό,
small husk, thin peel, etc., Hp. Nat.Puer. 22 , Arist. HA 546b20 , Theoc. 5.95 ;
egg-shell, Hp. Nat.Puer. 13 .

λεύκ-ανσις,εως,ἡ,
a growing white, Arist. Ph. 224b15 , Alex.Aphr. in Top. 304.1 ;
clarificationof oil, Gal. 11.484 .

Λίνδος,ἡ, the town ofLindos, Il. 2.656 , etc.:—Adv. Λινδόθεν
from Lindos, Call. Aet.Oxy. 2080.49 :—henceΛινδιᾰκος,ὁ(sc.λόγος), Chron.Lind.B 65 ;Λίνδιος,α,ον,Lindian, SIG 129.38 , al.;Ἀθάνα Λινδίαib. 725.11 ;Λινδιασταί,οἱ, religious guild at Lindos, IG 12(1).161 ;Λινδοπολίτας,α,ὁ,
citizen of Lindos, SIG 725.12 .

λῐπό-δερμος,ον,
without a skin, of ulcers, ibid.;
without a foreskin, Sor. 1.103 ;
circumcised, Dsc. 2.82 , Crito ap. Gal. 12.449 , Gal. 19.445 , Paul.Aeg. 6.53 .

λῐφαιμ-έω,
lack blood, Arist. Pr. 877a30 , Gal. 12.693 ;
bleed to death, J. AJ 8.15.5 , App. Gall. 10 , Hsch.

λῐ́φαιμ-ος,ον,
lacking blood, Emp. 100.1 ;
pallid, Hp. Mul. 2.119 , 125 .

λοπ-άω, (λοπός)
let the bark peel off, of trees which lose their bark on the return of the sap in spring, Thphr. HP 3.5.1 , 5.1.1 , etc. of fig-trees,
rot at the root, Id. CP 5.9.9 .

λοφ-εῖον,τό,
crestcase, Ar. Ach. 1109 ;
any case, Id. Nu. 751 .
